(CV Sorting using LLMs \(Capstone_Project-CS[02]\)) Tj
T*
(Student ID: m0b0xhj) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(This project implements an automated CV ranking system that scores candidate resumes) Tj
T*
(against a job description using two free local large language models \(llama3.2 and) Tj
T*
(gemma2\) served by Ollama. Resumes in TXT/PDF/DOCX are parsed into structured text, each) Tj
T*
(model produces an evidence-based fit score with strengths and gaps, and the scores are) Tj
T*
(aggregated into a transparent ranked list. The design is modular and plug-and-play: LLM) Tj
T*
(providers, parsers, and ranking logic are separable. A mock provider enables offline) Tj
T*
(testing of edge cases without a GPU.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(Recruiters spend significant time manually comparing resumes to role requirements.) Tj
T*
(Keyword filters miss context, while closed commercial APIs raise cost and privacy) Tj
T*
(concerns. This capstone builds a terminal-first ranking pipeline using open models that) Tj
T*
(can run locally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Problem Statement) Tj
T*
(Given a job description and a set of candidate CVs, produce a ranked list with) Tj
T*
(explainable match scores that reflect skills, experience, education, and responsibility) Tj
T*
(alignment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Objectives) Tj
T*
(- Parse CVs and job descriptions from common document formats.) Tj
T*
(- Use at least two LLMs \(llama3.2 + gemma2\) with justified dual scoring.) Tj
T*
(- Aggregate model outputs into a stable ranked list with explanations.) Tj
T*
(- Keep the codebase simple, testable, and free of LangChain complexity.) Tj
T*
(- Support plug-and-play LLM backends and offline mock evaluation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Methodology) Tj
T*
(Tools: Python 3, Ollama, pypdf, requests. No LangChain.) Tj
T*
(Workflow: parse JD -> parse CVs -> prompt each LLM -> parse JSON scores -> weighted) Tj
T*
(aggregate -> rank -> export JSON + console table.) Tj
T*
(Modules: config.py, parsers.py, prompts.py, llm_client.py \(OllamaProvider /) Tj
T*
(MockLLMProvider\), matcher.py, ranker.py, main.py.) Tj
T*
(Model justification: llama3.2 provides strong general instruction following for) Tj
T*
(structured JSON scoring; gemma2 adds a second open-weight judgment to reduce) Tj
T*
(single-model bias. Equal weights \(0.5/0.5\) keep aggregation interpretable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Results and Analysis) Tj
T*
(On the sample corpus \(Alice/Bob/Cara vs Senior Python Backend JD\), mock dual-model) Tj
T*
(ranking places Python/backend-aligned profiles above a Java/finance profile. With) Tj
T*
(--required-skills kubernetes, Cara ranks first due to explicit Kubernetes evidence. Unit) Tj
T*
(tests cover 40+ cases: empty/corrupt files, invalid LLM JSON, provider failures,) Tj
T*
(tie-breaking, and skill-filter refinement.) Tj
ET
